A||||4||mshill||V6 tube from valve cover to intake...||||5||
Z||000000||mshill||03-14-2000||03:16 PM||||On my 86SE V6 there is a solid tube from the front (firewall) valve cover to the rubber air intake tube between the filter and the throttle body.  Hint: It is not the PVC valve.  The strange thing is that I have an 86GT as well and it does not have one of these tubes.  I know it is obviously a breather for the valve cover, but why doesn't my GT have one?  Is it necessary?  Can I block off both holes?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||ka4nkf||03-14-2000||03:25 PM||||This was a recall item. The tube origanally ran from the valve cover to a tube along the firewall. they changed it and ran the tube from the valve cover to the air intake. Maybe your GT did not get the recall work.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||03-14-2000||03:31 PM||||Check the GT to see if it has a tube running from the valve cover to a tube on the firewall that runs to the air cleaner. This was the original design. The re-routing of the tube to the air intake tube was part of a recall.<P>My guess is the GT has not had the recall done. I think the recall included a new firewall side exhaust manifold. You might want to check into getting it done.<P>I thinks some sort of venting is required. I wouldn't plug it...<P>Here's a link with the recall info: <BR> <A HREF="http://www.tir.com/~jaski/v6recall.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tir.com/~jaski/v6recall.htm</A><P>ka4nkf, it took me so long to type you posted in between  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> <p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 03-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||mshill||03-14-2000||06:17 PM||||DRH, yes indeed it does go to that tube on the firewall.  I will have to give the PMCARES people a call to see what work can be done.<P>It's a real drag if the recall work needs to be done.  This car is in very poor repair, and I was going to repair the mechanical stuff prior to removing the panels for a kit car conversion.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||03-15-2000||03:57 PM||||If your front manifold is cracked, I've heard that it will be replaced as part of the recall. Might save you some time and $$.<BR>If you still have the weather seal along the front edge of the decklid (next to the glass), remove it before you have the recall done. It was normally removed and trashed as part of the recall. (A bad idea, IMHO.) If you leave it on, it will be gone when you get the car back.||||reg||1
